## Bitcoin Core `sighash.json`

`src/legacy_kat_vectors.zig` reproduces the official legacy (pre-segwit)
`SignatureHash()` reference-oracle corpus published by the Bitcoin Core
project at `src/test/data/sighash.json` (`bitcoin/bitcoin`, tag **`v29.0`**).
The file holds 501 array entries, one of them a header comment, so **500 data
rows — and all 500 are vendored**, unfiltered. Each row's `raw_transaction` /
`script` / `input_index` / `hashType` / `signature_hash` is transcribed by
`scripts/gen/gen-bitcoin-core-vectors.py`, never hand-typed.

## Bitcoin Core `tx_valid.json` + `tx_invalid.json`

`src/tx_wire_vectors.zig` reproduces every transaction in both files
(`bitcoin/bitcoin`, tag **`v29.0`**) as a wire-format corpus for this module's
serializer and deserializer: `tx_valid.json` contributes 120 data rows of its
247 entries, `tx_invalid.json` 93 of its 201, for **213 transactions**. Same
upstream, same MIT terms, same generator. It was not named in this file until
2026-09-09.

## Bitcoin Core `bip143`/`bip341` and the block-170 transaction

`src/bip143_kat_vectors.zig`, `src/bip341_kat_vectors.zig` and the `segwit_*`
entries of `src/tx_kat_vectors.zig` come from the BIPs' own published worked
examples (`bip-0143.mediawiki`, `bip-0341/wallet-test-vectors.json`) rather
than from Core. The `legacy_*` entries of `src/tx_kat_vectors.zig` are the
block-170 P2PK transaction, fetched from a block explorer — bytes the Bitcoin
network established, not anyone's authored corpus.

## python-bitcoinlib (LGPL-3.0) — an ORACLE, and nothing is taken from it

**Copyleft:** NONE-SHIPPED — python-bitcoinlib is an ORACLE this repository RUNS
at generation time, not code it ships: `scripts/gen/gen-bitcointx-single-bug.py`
builds its own transactions and reads back only the value
`RawSignatureHash` returns for them, so no python-bitcoinlib source and no
python-bitcoinlib data is in this repository, and nothing links against it.

`src/single_bug_kat_vectors.zig` names an **LGPL-3.0** library, so it is worth
saying plainly why no copyleft term reaches this collection — root `NOTICE` §1
makes copyleft in shipped material a defect to be removed, not a paperwork item,
so "no term reaches us" has to be demonstrated rather than assumed.

`scripts/gen/gen-bitcointx-single-bug.py` builds its transactions ITSELF — `mk(n_in,
n_out)` assembles inputs from `COutPoint(lx('aa'*32 …))` and outputs from
`CScript(bytes([0x51 + i]))`, all of it our own construction — and takes from
the library only the RETURN VALUE of `RawSignatureHash` on those inputs. That is
the black-box oracle case root `NOTICE` §0 carves out: the observable behaviour
of a program on our own input. No python-bitcoinlib source is read, ported or
shipped, and the library is not linked into anything this repository
distributes. Recorded here because the fact was true but nowhere written, which
is how a reader ends up re-deriving it.

