No Bitcoin Core C++ source is present in this module. The legacy sighash
algorithm itself is clean-room from Bitcoin Core's documented reference
behavior (there is no BIP for it — see `sighash_legacy.zig`'s module doc
comment and `SPEC.md`'s "Verification" section). What is reproduced here, and
only here, is conformance DATA — which is precisely why the notice lives
beside it.

This module's BIP143/BIP341 signature-hashing tests are anchored against
public BIP/spec-published examples (`bip-0143.mediawiki`, `bip-0341/
wallet-test-vectors.json`), which are not third-party CODE or DATA in the
sense this file exists to flag — see this module's `README.md` `Provenance:`
statement for that design reference instead.

